    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### qTox Version\n\nv1.18.2-76-g312699f34, v1.18.2 - stable release too, netify build too\n\n### Commit Hash\n\n312699f349c5ebff4df11b764767bdd1419c9094\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n0.2.20\n\n### Qt Version\n\n6.8.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start qTox\n2. Open Settings → About or Privacy\n3. Take a look at the textareas/large text fields \n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nThey are missing the right border. Probably platform specific.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5b8c0411-b2b3-4519-8029-901c80adb572)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7e075da6-1ffc-4450-b520-6ede4f9feddc)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/63d1ead5-9980-49c5-bd3d-0da382f1b472)\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nShould have right border.\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlways\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nWindows 10, 22H2\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\n\n```\n\nEdit: Add netify build to affected versions",
